When Hadoop starts, RHIPE wil launch an R process with the environment hadoop starts with.
This might  not contain a library search path that includes your libraries. One thing you could try is this

mapred = list( LD_LIBRARY_PATH=" /apps/rhel5/protobuf-2.3.0/lib: /usr/lib64/:/apps/coates/gcc-4.4.0/lib64: /apps/rhel5/R-2.11.1/lib64/R/lib/")

options(width=300)
map <- expression({
  for(x in map.values)
    rhcollect(x,runif(x))
})
z <- rhmr(map=map, N=10, inout=c("lapply","sequence"),ofolder="/wsc/tmp/sg2"

                ,mapred=append(mapred,list(mapred.map.tasks=2,mapred.reduce.tasks=0)))

rhex(z)

See if that works.

Cheers
Saptarshi

